Package: ventulus-diag
Architecture: all
# DEC-503: the whole Python library and the ventulus-diag program, without the
# Qt stack, so a machine with no desktop can run the diagnostics. Up to 5.5.x
# these files were the ventulus package's: Breaks and Replaces let them move
# here when one of those is upgraded (Debian Policy 7.6.1). Any older ventulus
# is broken by this build in fact, since each depends on its own ventulus-diag
# (= its version); apt upgrades the two together.
# The floors are pyproject.toml's; ventulusd's is constants.DAEMON_MINIMUM_VERSION
# (tests/test_packaging_linux.py holds both equal).
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.12),
 ventulusd (>= 3.0.0),
 python3-httpx (>= 0.27)
Breaks: ventulus (<< ${binary:Version})
Replaces: ventulus (<< ${binary:Version})
Description: Diagnostics for the Ventulus fan control daemon
 ventulus-diag runs the tests that deliberately drive fans for investigation:
 the PWM Test Report, PWM characterisation, control-path discovery and
 validation sessions. Each is a ventulusd diagnostic, which the daemon checks,
 performs and undoes; the tool asks for confirmation before anything changes
 a fan speed. It needs no desktop.

Package: ventulus
Architecture: all
# The floors are pyproject.toml's (tests/test_packaging_linux.py holds them
# equal); ventulusd's is constants.DAEMON_MINIMUM_VERSION. pyqtgraph imports
# QtOpenGL, and without qt6-svg-plugins the app icon is blank (DEC-499 phase 0).
# gpg verifies the signed update manifest. gpg-agent too: Debian's gpg 2.4
# exits 2 on --import when it cannot start the agent, even though the key
# imported, and the update check refuses any non-zero exit.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.12),
 ventulus-diag (= ${binary:Version}),
 ventulusd (>= 3.0.0),
 python3-pyside6.qtcore (>= 6.6), python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets,
 python3-pyside6.qtnetwork, python3-pyside6.qtopengl, python3-pyside6.qtopenglwidgets,
 qt6-svg-plugins, python3-pyqtgraph (>= 0.13.7), python3-numpy (>= 1:2.0),
 python3-httpx (>= 0.27), python3-colorama (>= 0.4), gpg, gpg-agent,
 hicolor-icon-theme
Description: Desktop GUI for the Ventulus fan control daemon
 Ventulus shows the fans and temperatures ventulusd reads and edits the
 fan profiles it runs: curves, roles, overrides and fan tests. It talks only
 to the daemon, over its local socket; the daemon alone drives the hardware
 and keeps the fans under control when the GUI is closed.
